examples.question_text:
The graph shows the cost of hiring a bicycle, including a booking fee. Use the graph to find the cost of hiring it for $3$ hours.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=6,ymin=0,ymax=40,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,5,...,40},grid=major,grid style={draw={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204}},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={Time (hours)},ylabel={Cost (dollars)}]
\addplot[thick,black,domain=0:6,samples=2]{5*x+5};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=6,ymin=0,ymax=40,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,5,...,40},grid=major,grid style={draw={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204}},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={Time (hours)},ylabel={Cost (dollars)}]
\addplot[thick,black,domain=0:6,samples=2]{5*x+5};
\addplot[dashed,color={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] coordinates {(3,0) (3,20) (0,20)};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,mark size=2pt,color={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] coordinates {(3,20)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
From $x=3$, move vertically to the line, then horizontally to the cost axis. The graph gives $y=20$.
Hiring the bicycle for $3$ hours costs $\$20$.
